  "limitations": [
    "One model family and one recipe. scGPT's own published perturbation recipe on the screen the question is about is the strongest single test available, but another architecture or objective could behave differently.",
    "The main arms score two of five folds, which resolves a paired difference more coarsely than run 3's five; on these folds co-expression is not separated from the shuffled-label band either. The cross-fitted variant covers the whole screen and agrees.",
    "Fine-tuning and evaluation come from the same screen, split by response group. That is the published setting and the one most favourable to the model; it says nothing about fine-tuning on a different screen.",
    "The response features are read at run 3's primary anchor. Run 3 swept four anchors on the frozen model and none lifted the features out of the band, but that sweep was not repeated on every fine-tuned checkpoint.",
    "A null is bounded by what the measurement resolves. The shuffled-label band and the achieved resolution of each paired difference are reported next to every number so the size of an effect that would have been missed is visible."
  ],
